* Zama coprocessor
** Four responsibilities
*** Compute FHE ops from executor events
*** Verify and attest encrypted inputs
*** Commit ciphertext digests to the Gateway
*** Serve ciphertexts to the KMS from S3
** Six services around PostgreSQL
*** host-listener + poller: events to dependence chains
*** gw-listener: input requests to verify_proofs
*** tfhe-worker: TFHE-rs evaluation, leased chains
*** zkproof-worker: ZKPoK check, handles
*** sns-worker: switch-and-squash, S3, digests
*** tx-sender: EIP-712 attestation + Gateway txs
** Data path
*** Executor event to computations row
*** Evaluate once inputs exist
*** Allowed event to squash and upload
*** addCiphertextMaterial, majority consensus
*** KMS downloads and checks digest
** Infrastructure (coprocessor-operator)
*** EKS, Karpenter pools: 88 CPU FHE nodes
*** RDS PostgreSQL, ExternalName service
*** S3 behind Cloudflare hostname
*** AWS KMS secp256k1 signing key
*** hub.zama.org images, Grafana Cloud
** Deployment steps
*** secrets-bootstrap.sh
*** DB roles job
*** operator-check pre-flight hook
*** One Helm values file per release
*** Key import to KMS
** Operating
*** Cursors, replay, seed-start-block
*** Slow lane, unlimited commitment retries
*** Blue-green upgrade with state hashes
@endmindmap
